# YesWeCheck API: every request, ready to send.
# VS Code: install the REST Client extension, export YWC_API_KEY, then click "Send Request".
# JetBrains IDEs: put your key on the @apiKey line below (and don't commit it).

@baseUrl = https://api.yeswecheck.fr
@apiKey = {{$processEnv YWC_API_KEY}}

### Verify · Verify an address
# Runs every check enabled on your key and returns a verdict: `valid`, `risky`, `invalid` or `unknown`.
# 1 credit if your key has SMTP enabled and the verdict is not `unknown`. Otherwise free.
# @name validate
POST {{baseUrl}}/v2/email/validate
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept-Language: en-GB
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@company.co.uk"
}

### Verify · Verify with a reference country
# `country` sets the reference country for the presumed age (ISO 3166-1). `smtpTimeout` caps the wait for the remote mail server, in milliseconds (1,000–30,000).
# @name validate-country
POST {{baseUrl}}/v2/email/validate
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept-Language: en-GB
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@company.co.uk",
  "country": "GB",
  "smtpTimeout": 10000
}

### Verify · Enrich an address
# First name, last name, gender and presumed age guessed from the address. Free: no credit used.
# @name enrich
POST {{baseUrl}}/v2/email/enrich
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept-Language: en-GB
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@company.co.uk",
  "country": "GB"
}

### Suggest · Detect a typo
# Suggests a fix for a mistyped domain. Send `email` or `domain`. Free: no credit used.
# @name typo
POST {{baseUrl}}/v2/email/suggest/typo-domain
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept-Language: en-GB
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane@gmial.com"
}

### Suggest · Suggest domains
# Domain autocomplete after the `@`, ranked by popularity in the country. Free: no credit used.
# @name domains
POST {{baseUrl}}/v2/email/suggest/domain
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept-Language: en-GB
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "partial": "gm",
  "country": "GB",
  "count": 5
}

### Suggest · List covered countries
# Countries with a dedicated domain ranking. Free: no credit used.
# @name countries
GET {{baseUrl}}/v2/email/suggest/domain/countries
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept-Language: en-GB

### Suggest · Generate local parts
# Likely local parts for a person (`jane.doe`, `jdoe`…). With `domain`, each suggestion carries the full address. Free: no credit used.
# @name localpart
POST {{baseUrl}}/v2/email/suggest/localpart?domain=company.co.uk
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept-Language: en-GB
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "maxResults": 5
}

### Suggest · Autocomplete a first name
# Free: no credit used.
# @name first-name
POST {{baseUrl}}/v2/email/suggest-firstname
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept-Language: en-GB
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "Oli",
  "limit": 5
}

### Suggest · Autocomplete a last name
# Free: no credit used.
# @name last-name
POST {{baseUrl}}/v2/email/suggest-lastname
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept-Language: en-GB
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "Smi",
  "limit": 5
}

### Account · Organisation, balance and key
# Your credit balance, the key's settings and its usage against its caps. Free: no credit used.
# @name me
GET {{baseUrl}}/v2/me
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept-Language: en-GB

### Account · Plan catalogue
# Plans and credit packs, with prices. No key needed.
# @name catalog
GET {{baseUrl}}/v2/billing/catalog
Accept-Language: en-GB

### Status · API status
# No key needed.
# @name health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept-Language: en-GB
